-- Talking: `when player talks to "wizard"` fires on the frame the TALK key goes down
-- while the player overlaps the wizard (the keys file presses space on frame 2), and
-- the handler shows a dialog plus two choices. The dialog box + choice buttons are
-- engine-emitted commands, so per-frame parity covers them.
player is {x: 40, y: 40}
wizard is {x: 44, y: 40}
wizard are talkers
said is 0
when player talks to "wizard"
  said is said + 1
  show dialog "Hello, traveler!" at 2, 92
  show choice "ask about quest" "leave" at 4, 60
to update
  tick is 1
to draw
  clear screen to dark blue
  draw sprite player at player.x, player.y
  draw sprite wizard at wizard.x, wizard.y
  if dialog is not "" write "said {said}" at 2, 2 in white on hud
  if choice is not "" write "pick {choice}" at 2, 12 in yellow on hud
run game with update and draw
